                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game. Oh boy, this game. Just don't even bother. Simple as that. Here is why:\nIt is broken. The mouse controls are just down right broken. I could only continue playing this because I have an Xbox controller to plug in. Even then, this game is barely playable. The physics...make no sense. For some reason you accelerate while going up a hill and the cart doesn't decelerate at the peak of the hill. This can be level breaking in some levels in which you have to stop or you will fall off. \nThe first chapter has 30 levels and the second chapter has 9. Did they forget how to count? I haven't finish the game and so I do not know how many levels are in the third and final \"Event\", but at this rate it might be around 3. It seems that as the game development progressed, they just completely gave up.\nSpeaking of giving up, there are a few levels that made me laugh. Stage 2-8 comes to mind. This level seems utterly impossible. If you travel slowly, you fail. If you travel quickly, you fail. Also, really a gem under the track? Was there a misclick when level editing? If you slow down enough to suck in that strangely placed gem, then you will get hit by the boulders.\nThe fucking gems. Half my playtime was me idling as I rubbed my temples, breathing in and out slowly, and redoing levels because the hitbox radius on the vehicle is ♥♥♥♥ing broken. I literally passed over collectible gems, they entered my body, and then they quickly shot out of me for no apparent reason. This causes you to redo levels just because a gem decided that this day wasn't its day to be collected.\nThe art. Is it art? I am getting a bit sick of these low effort pixelated games on Steam. Some are really well done. Most aren't. The colors and contrast in this game is bad. There is no sense of a color palette. Every pixel just blends in together and it is very hard to focus on things.\nThe UI is pretty funny. When I tell you that a word is greyed out, you would think that means locked or unclickable right? Nope, grey words are the main things you click on. White words are...I am not even sure. Just info and random words on the side I guess.\nThe main menu tells you how bad this game is. Watch the drivers, 9/10 don't make it over the fist gap. When the physics don't even work in the main menu, you know you are in for some bullshit in the actual levels.\nAnyway I could honestly go on and on about how awful this game is. The only positives are that I like the customization options and the gem bank mechanic where collectible turn into usable money. But everything else sucks. This game is broken, ugly, and not fun. Don't bother.",
